Add the missing DataSource.get_seq_length() to DeformableEnvDataSource.

rollout.py (and the sliced-dataset headroom filter) calls
data_source.get_seq_length(traj_idx), which DeformableEnvDataSource omits (the
abstract base does not enforce it), so DINO-WM rope/granular long-rollout crashes
with AttributeError. self.seq_lengths is already populated in __init__ (fixed
length per trajectory), so this mirrors the sibling PushT/DinoWorldModel impls.

--- a/src/wm_datasets/data_source/dino_wm/deformable.py
+++ b/src/wm_datasets/data_source/dino_wm/deformable.py
@@ -102,6 +102,9 @@
     def get_num_trajectories(self) -> int:
         return self.num_trajectories
 
+    def get_seq_length(self, index: int) -> int:
+        return int(self.seq_lengths[index].item())
+
     @property
     def action_dim(self) -> int:
         return self._action_dim
